{
  "name": "tj-binomheap",
  "description": "A Rust implementation of the binomial heap data structure, providing a mergeable priority queue with O(log n) worst-case performance for most operations. The library represents the heap as a forest of binomial trees where the presence of a tree of order 'k' corresponds to the k-th bit in the binary representation of the total element count. This structural property enables heap merges to be implemented as a binary addition analogy over the underlying tree sequence.",
